{"question_id":"mnswhpuh","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift","year":2026,"subject":"physics","chapter":"units-and-measurements","chapterGroup":"mechanics","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"content":"<p>In a Vernier calipers, when both jaws touch each other, zero of the Vernier scale is shifted to the right of zero of the main scale and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.199ex\" height=\"2.071ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -893.3 1855.8 915.3\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"37\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-37\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(533,363) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">th\u00a0</text></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Vernier division coincides with a main scale reading. If the value of 1 main scale division is 1 mm and there are 10 Vernier scale divisions, then the Vernier caliper has</p>\n","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<p>0.07 cm negative zero error</p>\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"<p>0.7 cm negative zero error</p>\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"<p>0.07 cm positive zero error</p>\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"<p>0.7 cm positive zero error</p>"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<p>The Least Count is the smallest measurement that can be accurately taken using the instrument.</p>\n<p>For a Vernier calliper, the difference between the length of one Main Scale Division (MSD) and one Vernier Scale Division (VSD) is equal to the least count.</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20.837ex\" height=\"1.781ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 9210 787\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4C\"></use><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\" transform=\"translate(625,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1624.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2680.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(3180.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4D\"></use><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\" transform=\"translate(917,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"44\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-44\" transform=\"translate(1473,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(5639.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(6640,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(7140,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"56\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-56\"></use><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"44\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-44\" transform=\"translate(1306,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>It is given that <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.452ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"15.467ex\" height=\"2.149ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 6836.6 950\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4D\"></use><use data-c=\"53\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-53\" transform=\"translate(917,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"44\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-44\" transform=\"translate(1473,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3014.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(4070.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(4570.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">\u00a0</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(600,0)\"><use data-c=\"6D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6D\"></use><use data-c=\"6D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6D\" transform=\"translate(833,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>.</p>\n<p>In a standard Vernier calliper arrangement, 10 divisions on the Vernier scale correspond to the length of 9 divisions on the Main scale.</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16.155ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 7140.6 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-